IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 5033 of 2021
CITATION: (2022) 6 SCC 496
YEAR: 2022

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: D.Y. Chandrachud, A.S. Bopanna

PARTIES:
Vodafone Idea vs Ajay Kumar Agarwal

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Consumer Protection Act, 1986, Indian Telegraph Act, 1885

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 7B Telegraph Act, Section 3 Consumer Protection

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
telecom consumer complaints, consumer forum jurisdiction, remedies not barred

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Held that consumer disputes against telecom service providers are maintainable before consumer forums despite Section 7B of the Indian Telegraph Act.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 7B Telegraph Act, Section 3 Consumer Protection.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

